WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:14.600
We'll be right back.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:56.660
Yes, it's new.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:04.940
I know. That's why I'm afraid. It's so delicate.

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:07.010
It's preferable that you caress it.

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:09.380
Come on, dear.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:15.550
- Is there danger? - None.

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:16.800
Then let's see it.

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:20.100
Get out of my way, dear.

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:54.580
And if you're lucky, he'll make you kiss his feet, the waters and kiss you, I can't

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.650
I swim to the river to wash you

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:10.650
Envy because they kiss the rose of your face

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:15.530
Envy because they kiss the rose of your face

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:18.530
Oh, lemon of the lemoner, oh, orange of Nahal

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:22.530
Oh, this pretty girl, what I saw was my sorrow

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:26.540
Oh, sweetness of your orange and acidity of your lemon

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:30.000
In these green leaves I want to put my love

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:48.730
I'm going to put that canela in the branch, daughter of my soul!

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:52.790
- People can't come, right? - Who's going to come out of the hour?

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:56.210
Study quietly. I'm going to mark the clock.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:30.000
Oh, my God.

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:34.290
that the water is not as sweet as a penne, she knows how to swim

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:02.020
I want to go home.

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:35.900
Oh, my God, Moros.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.100
Moros, my daughter, Moros.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:03.890
- Who's running there? - They're mice!

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:09.400
- Stop! Stop! - Oh, it's you.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:12.440
- Yes, it's me. What's going on? - That's what I'm asking.

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:14.290
What's the saleswoman doing here, out of time,

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:16.290
wasting the company's pianos, breaking the records,

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.290
and hiding in the corridors?

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:20.290
She doesn't break, she doesn't spend, and she hides.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:22.150
She was rehearsing because I gave her permission.

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:25.150
- And who are you to give her permission? - A house employee, just like you.

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:29.060
And after all this, why do we have to give you so many explanations?

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:34.220
tomorrow, Mr. Paco, and thank you very much. The explanations will be given tomorrow in front of our superiors.

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:37.200
You run to tell him tonight, that maybe he will give you a

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:43.050
gaita for how well you blow. I never expected such an act of indiscipline, Mr. Paco.

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:47.080
On the other hand, I expected anything from you.

00:07:47.080 --> 00:08:00.000
Shall we open the floor or raise the screen? Why don't you talk? I have everything

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.920
- You're the manager, right? - But you're the bosses, unfortunately!

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:08.040
- How, unfortunately? - Yes, sir, because if your parents lived...

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:09.850
...things wouldn't be like this.

00:08:09.850 --> 00:08:14.290
Don Pedro and Don Roque Vulcano sacrificed years to raise the prestige of the firm.

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:17.490
- And all for what? - So that their respective and meritorious sons...

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:20.450
...will throw the house into the water like a slide.

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:23.450
- We're on a shipwreck. - Why didn't you record it?

00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:25.070
- What? - This bolero.

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:26.640
Every day he's going to sing the same thing.

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:30.000
All I want is to save them from the shipwreck.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.400
But you don't listen to me, and if we continue like this, soon the water will reach our knees.

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:36.880
With the water to the knees, no one drowns.

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:39.580
But we are head down.

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:42.100
The house has more tenants than customers.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:45.260
Last month we broke an extraordinary record.

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:47.720
- Really? - Of discos without selling.

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:50.130
And now you solve it, you are the manager, look for a solution.

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.850
- There is only one solution. - Which one?

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:53.970
Ten liters of naphtha and a phosphor.

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:56.430
It's useless, sir, you can't talk to him, he's always pessimistic.

00:08:56.430 --> 00:09:00.000
- We have hope, mountains of hope. - And oceans of hope!

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.250
Debt! Where are we going to drown?

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:04.390
The water doesn't reach us here.

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:14.280
- Let's go. - And, what do you think?

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:16.340
- What? - About the water and the post.

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:18.720
Impossible. We don't have water insurance.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.440
- ABC. - Madrid.

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:29.510
- I'll take care of it. - Hello?

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:34.310
Niní, what a surprise, dear. What are you doing?

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:37.520
Waiting for me to confirm the time of the recording of tonight.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:41.330
- You forgot again. - No, no, no, dear, no. What hope?

00:09:41.570 --> 00:09:43.700
- Look, what happens is that... - What?

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:47.320
- Another recording with Niní? - Please, please.

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:51.050
Listen, dear, there are certain technical difficulties.

00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:54.900
No difficulties. Either I record tonight or the lawyer intervenes.

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:58.040
Businesses have nothing to do with love.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.000
I demand the fulfillment of my contract.

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:09.900
Famous contracts, your sensational discovery.

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:11.340
Mimi, the doll from Paris.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:13.500
We have a deposit full of her albums without selling them.

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:16.340
- That's lack of publicity. - It's lack of shame, don't you see?

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:18.820
You're the one who takes the cork out of the bottom of the bottle to make it sink.

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:20.940
I don't take the cork out of anyone. I look for Alexis.

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:24.260
But you look for her in return, like with Dalila, the palm tree that sings.

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:25.900
And the Sister Menendez.

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:30.000
And Rosana Rosana, who you made record the scene of the madness of Luciana Mermur, accompanied by...

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.300
At least I'm worried. I'm looking for the novelty.

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:35.300
While you remain indifferent, reading foreign magazines.

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:39.660
- Can you come in? - What do you want?

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:42.660
Forgive the intrusion. It's about something important.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:44.660
- Miss Isabel de Castro. - Who?

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:47.570
Isabel de Castro. The saleswoman number four.

00:10:47.570 --> 00:10:51.610
Last night, I came in without staying here and I surprised her.

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:54.110
Look, I was with the records, then I played the piano.

00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:56.110
- Isabel! - Huh?

00:10:56.110 --> 00:11:00.000
- What a nice desk. - So, can I say goodbye?

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.460
If they kick you out, I'll go too.

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:03.860
In other words, it's the most boring job I've ever had in my life.

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:06.240
Yes, but at least we were in our environment.

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:07.890
Near the music, the art.

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:11.140
Yes, shaking the dust off the discs that no one comes to buy, they kick us out.

00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:14.470
You know that at home you will never miss a meal.

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:17.070
Yes, but I can't become a parasite of your family.

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:19.810
Well, well, well, then let's look for a job in another house and that's it.

00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:23.910
Look, they'll kick me out of here.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:27.080
But I'll put that Arcontreras inside a piano.

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:30.000
As faithful servant of the house, I saw myself obliged to inform him.

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:32.770
- What was that saleswoman's name? - Isabel de Castro, sir.

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:34.230
All right. Go on, Contreras.

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:38.290
Thank you, Mr. Vulcano. And you know, always to the orders of the firm.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:41.040
Thank you very much, sir. Thank you very much.

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:44.670
Where did I read that name?

00:11:44.860 --> 00:11:46.800
- What's wrong with you? - Isabel de...

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:54.560
Here it is. I found it here, in the ABC of Madrid.

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:57.080
- What? - Read this.

00:11:58.210 --> 00:11:59.640
"Herencia sin heredera."

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:02.200
is ignored by the fate of young millionaires.

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:06.690
The happy heir to a legacy of 20 million pesetas

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:08.730
has not been able to be located,

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:11.250
left testamentarily by the well-known philanthropist

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:13.290
recently deceased, Carmelo de Fuenzalida.

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:15.330
Albacía seeks the whereabouts of Isabel de Castro,

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:17.450
of 20 million pesetas, of 20 years of age,

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:19.570
favored with immense fortune,

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:23.690
of whom only it is known that she left for South America in 1945.

00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:25.970
Isabel de Castro.

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:30.000
Saleswoman number 4, 20 million pesetas.

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:31.640
I'll find out right away.

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:36.240
- Will you join the staff? - Yes, sir.

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:38.960
Congratulations, gentlemen!

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:40.790
News from the interior has just arrived.

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:42.830
Our headquarters in Córdoba and Tucumán have been closed.

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:45.610
The managers advise you to set up competition on the spot.

00:12:45.710 --> 00:12:46.990
What did I answer you?

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:50.630
- Solve it. You are the manager. - Manager, yes, but not a magician.

00:12:50.730 --> 00:12:52.110
All right, let it be. I'll study it later.

00:12:52.210 --> 00:12:53.830
There's no time, we're sinking!

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:55.910
Don't worry, we're going to find a life saver.

00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:58.740
As you say, but the water doesn't reach us here.

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:03.720
- Ara, did you call me over the phone? - Not until now, Mr. Contreras.

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:04.380
Thank you.

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:12.030
- Are you looking for him? - Yes, thank you.

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:15.300
Miss Isabel, you're being called from the Federal Directorate.

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:19.990
Hey, Isabel, come on. I'm going to attend to the gentleman.

00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:24.480
Resignation, courage, I'll be strong.

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:27.090
- Is something wrong? - No, but it's going to happen.

00:13:27.310 --> 00:13:29.760
Just a moment.

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:34.020
- May I come in? - Come on in.

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:40.500
- May I come in? - Come in, miss.

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:44.730
- Are you Isabel de Castro? - Yes, sir. Saleswoman number 4.

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:46.880
- I'd like to tell you that last night... - Take a seat.

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:50.860
- Take a seat. - Please, sit down.

00:13:51.890 --> 00:14:00.000
- Sit down. - Sir, I'd like to tell you that last night...

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:02.400
Who is Isabel de Castro? Separated, right?

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:05.290
Single, sir.

00:14:05.660 --> 00:14:09.160
I mean the syllable "de". Isabel de Castro.

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:13.260
You weren't born here, were you?

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:16.460
No, sir. In Spain. But ten years ago I came to Buenos Aires.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:20.490
- Is it true that you traveled in...? - In 1945, sir.

00:14:20.690 --> 00:14:24.710
- And how old were you when you were born? - What did you say?

00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:27.110
I meant how old were you when you traveled?

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:30.000
- I turned ten years old on the ship. - And when did you arrive?

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:34.010
The same one, sir, that would have come to your office.

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:35.440
You mean that now you have...

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:37.270
Twenty, sir, but...

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:38.900
...so many questions are needed.

00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:41.400
Are they necessary to explain certain facts?

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:42.400
Precisely.

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:45.760
I wanted to explain that last night, the only indiscipline I did...

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:48.530
...was to come and rehearse my singing lessons after hours...

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:51.590
...without considering that that was a reason to say goodbye.

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:53.090
Say goodbye?

00:14:53.090 --> 00:14:55.090
Quite the opposite, Miss Isabel de Castro.

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:57.090
Why didn't you tell us that you studied singing?

00:14:57.090 --> 00:15:00.000
I... it's the first time I've spoken to you.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.920
- Because they always see their bosses as enemies. - There it is.

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:06.880
Let's see. What was the need to sacrifice yourself coming at night?

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:11.780
I'm poor, sir. I have no money at home.

00:15:11.780 --> 00:15:16.180
And what are we here for? To help you, to stimulate your vocation.

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:18.440
You have to look at it as if we were your brothers.

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:20.820
More than your brothers. Your parents.

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:25.570
- I can't imagine... - Tell me, miss.

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:30.000
If tomorrow we came to you to ask for your help, your help...

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:34.380
- For me? That would be funny. - And no one knows. Would you refuse?

00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:36.330
- No, I wouldn't. - Neither would we.

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:38.330
The Vulcano house is at your disposal.

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:42.330
Mario and Gerardo Vulcano, delighted to hear you sing.

00:15:42.430 --> 00:15:47.330
And the Vulcano record label, very honored to record a recording for you.

00:15:47.430 --> 00:15:52.260
- Record me? - Yes, miss.

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:56.110
- Tonight at ten o'clock in the living room. - No, no, no.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:16:00.000
- Tonight we have an orchestra and everything ready for you. - No, no, no.

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:06.150
- So we'll wait for you, eh? - Honestly, I can't find a word.

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:11.710
There's no need. We have faith in your youth, in your blooming 20 years.

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:13.420
- You were 20, right? - Yes, sir.

00:16:13.420 --> 00:16:16.220
- And you landed in 1945. - Yes, sir.

00:16:16.220 --> 00:16:18.600
Perfectly, Miss Isabel de Castro.

00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:20.940
- Your name was like that, right? - Yes, sir, yes.

00:16:20.940 --> 00:16:25.910
- You see how I don't forget? - I'll never forget this gesture.

00:16:25.910 --> 00:16:28.670
- That's how we'll wait for you. - Thank you.

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:30.000
- Excuse me. - Jesus.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:36.460
- That Nini records tonight. - She does.

00:16:36.460 --> 00:16:38.350
- She does. - Say my word.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:40.340
- Besides, there's a contract. - There's a new contract.

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:43.340
And I found a lifesaver called 20 million pesetas.

00:16:43.340 --> 00:16:46.340
Mario, think about it. We're between the sword and the wall. What do we do?

00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:48.160
- I don't know. - Break the wall.

00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:49.160
- And Nini breaks my head. - No, no, no.

00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:52.160
- I'll take care of her. No problem. - Why are you going to take care of yourself?

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:54.160
Because you're going to be very busy.

00:16:54.160 --> 00:17:00.000
You'll have to deploy all your artillery to conquer that divinity called 20 million pesetas.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:02.000
- 20 million pesetas. - You're crazy.

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.080
That's what they said to Pastel.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:06.080
And yet, he found the vaccine.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:09.040
I found Isabel, and she has to join the family.

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:12.040
I don't know if as a girlfriend, mother, wife, or adopted daughter.

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:16.640
But she has to join with her 20 million pesetas, and it all depends on you.

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:19.640
- Why does it depend on me? - Because I don't have Tenorio's soul.

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:21.640
On the other hand, you have your background.

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:24.500
You conquered Nini, Fischer, Rosanna.

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:27.620
The singers are your specialty.

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:30.000
The duo of the Menendez separated because of you.

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:33.490
There you have it, the gallery of your conquests against me.

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:36.490
- Make one, please. - No, I can't lend myself to that.

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:39.630
- I didn't lend you, I gave it to you. - It's useless, it's against my principles.

00:17:39.670 --> 00:17:41.670
Don't think about the principles, think about the endings.

00:17:42.300 --> 00:17:45.420
No! Good news, gentlemen, the lawyer has just spoken.

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:49.210
- Really? What did he say? - Ask him if we want it for this month or for next month.

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:50.610
- What? - The bankruptcy.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:53.300
Mario, it's all in your hands.

00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:58.000
I don't know, I'd have to think about it.

00:17:58.040 --> 00:18:00.000
Well, think about it quickly, because...

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:02.360
Gentlemen, this is the end of the story.

00:18:02.860 --> 00:18:07.060
I was waiting for the news of my marriage.

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:08.120
I still don't understand.

00:18:08.320 --> 00:18:12.120
Are you sure you've never been heard singing?

00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:13.180
Never.

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:16.290
- Not even by chance? - Not at all.

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:20.780
So, they've found out I'm your teacher.

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:22.300
I already said that.

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:23.820
And why the triumph?

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:25.620
The triumph is like the...

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:26.640
I don't know.

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:30.000
Because from time to time, but when you have it...

00:18:30.350 --> 00:18:33.240
- Jeremia, eat! - Yes, woman, yes, yes.

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:36.820
I have some nerves.

00:18:36.820 --> 00:18:40.370
- Do you want to eat? - No, Mrs. Marta, I can't.

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:42.000
- I'm scared. - Of what?

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:44.800
- Of doing a bad role. - Doing a bad role?

00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:47.200
But you know everything you need to know.

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:51.460
Because singing is, how would I say it, as soon as you understand the...

00:18:51.460 --> 00:18:54.200
But no, Jeremia, for God's sake, a recording is something else.

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:57.330
Microphone, musician, lights that turn on and chicharras that sound,

00:18:57.330 --> 00:19:00.000
and I'm so scared that I keep my mouth open without saying a word.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.000
I don't know where to stop.

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:02.000
You stop here.

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:03.000
Give me the microphone.

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:04.000
What microphone?

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:05.000
The telephone, woman.

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:06.000
The orchestra will be there.

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:30.000
Let's go to Formago.

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:54.840
The great whiteness was like a goddess's bath, dreams of art towards another country. It was like a creme de la creme.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:29.250
They are the Vulcans.

00:20:30.860 --> 00:20:31.910
I don't see them.

00:20:32.380 --> 00:20:35.820
They'll be in a special cabin, so they can listen quietly.

00:20:36.220 --> 00:20:38.380
No, no and no! I want an orchestra!

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:40.900
But, Nini, Maestro Silva is superior to an orchestra.

00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:43.420
My contrast says I have to record with 30 teachers.

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:45.700
- But he's worth 40, right? - You won't convince me.

00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:48.740
But, Nini, be good, be sensible, think about the propaganda.

00:20:48.820 --> 00:20:51.540
His figure coming out of a piano with a rain of musical notes

00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:53.100
that slip through his body.

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:54.560
I don't trust you.

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:56.850
Silence! Silence!

00:20:57.220 --> 00:21:00.000
I have the solution. The great solution.

00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:04.580
Nini, my dear little girl, we'll make another contract.

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:06.410
I can't believe it.

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:09.700
I toast to our dinner.

00:21:09.820 --> 00:21:12.870
Tonight is good, with Spanish wine.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:15.910
And I came...

00:21:32.650 --> 00:21:42.290
Oh

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:07.360
Very good. Congratulations, Miss.

00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:08.360
Thank you very much.

00:22:08.360 --> 00:22:10.360
Wonderful, my child, wonderful!

00:22:10.360 --> 00:22:11.360
Despite the orchestra.

00:22:11.360 --> 00:22:12.860
What does the orchestra have?

00:22:12.860 --> 00:22:15.360
You will see, at some point, the bass.

00:22:15.360 --> 00:22:16.360
Now, that's right.

00:22:16.360 --> 00:22:20.360
When she raised the bass on the string of life.

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:21.360
Yes, Mr. Jeremia, yes.

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:23.360
Did you like the Burkans?

00:22:23.360 --> 00:22:26.450
Did you like the song?

00:22:26.450 --> 00:22:27.750
What?

00:22:27.750 --> 00:22:28.950
Are you done?

00:22:28.950 --> 00:22:29.960
Yes, Mr. Burkana.

00:22:30.510 --> 00:22:32.180
You have a brilliant future.

00:22:32.180 --> 00:22:34.870
- What do you think? - A future we'll share happily.

00:22:34.870 --> 00:22:37.250
We want to take care of your career, to walk it.

00:22:37.250 --> 00:22:38.990
I don't know how to thank you.

00:22:38.990 --> 00:22:41.790
Thank him. I have to avoid the death of a pianist.

00:22:41.790 --> 00:22:45.210
Excuse me, Miss Isabel, I have to tell you very important things.

00:22:45.210 --> 00:22:48.300
- I hear you, I hear you. - Yes, but not here, forgive me.

00:22:48.300 --> 00:22:51.340
I need to talk to you serenely, in a quiet place.

00:22:51.340 --> 00:22:53.700
- What do you think if we go alone to... - No, I can't.

00:22:53.700 --> 00:22:55.720
I can't leave my teacher and my friend.

00:22:55.720 --> 00:23:00.000
I'm going to introduce you to my teacher, my teacher, and my friend.

00:23:00.030 --> 00:23:02.050
- Mr. Vulcano. - Mario Vulcano, at your service.

00:23:02.070 --> 00:23:04.110
- Nice to meet you. - I'm delighted.

00:23:04.130 --> 00:23:06.450
- Mario! - Mimi, please, Mimi, please, Mimi!

00:23:06.470 --> 00:23:09.490
- Calm down, calm down. - Calm down, don't make fun of me.

00:23:09.510 --> 00:23:11.470
I want you to respect my status as a star.

00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:14.210
If I told you I'd have an 8-color poster with your name on it, I'd write it down.

00:23:14.230 --> 00:23:17.470
That aside, I want my recording with an artist and not with a crazy pianist!

00:23:17.490 --> 00:23:21.770
But how? Tomorrow, at any time, we'll say there were certain technical problems.

00:23:21.790 --> 00:23:24.850
Yes, ma'am, it's a copy of what we just recorded.

00:23:24.870 --> 00:23:26.230
- For me? - For you, yes.

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:27.330
Thank you very much, sir.

00:23:27.350 --> 00:23:29.520
So these are the technical problems.

00:23:29.540 --> 00:23:30.000
No, I don't want to.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:32.800
- Let's get out of here. - I don't want to make anyone record.

00:23:32.900 --> 00:23:35.330
- No, no. - What do you mean, anyone?

00:23:35.430 --> 00:23:37.490
Who are you? Who are you?

00:23:37.590 --> 00:23:40.310
I don't know you. And if I don't know you, you don't exist.

00:23:40.340 --> 00:23:42.200
On the other hand, I have a name, a cartel.

00:23:42.300 --> 00:23:44.200
No, no, it's an accidental commitment that we have...

00:23:44.300 --> 00:23:48.200
Excuse me, Mr. Burtano. I'm not an accident and you have a commitment to me.

00:23:48.300 --> 00:23:50.200
- But with me, yes. - Yes, with her, yes.

00:23:50.300 --> 00:23:52.060
And you came to steal my place.

00:23:52.160 --> 00:23:54.010
The place of Nini, Pearl's doll.

00:23:54.110 --> 00:23:58.020
I don't know if you know that I have recorded more than 50 songs.

00:23:58.120 --> 00:24:00.000
58.

00:24:00.030 --> 00:24:04.030
58,000 records that are dying of boredom in the shelves without anyone buying them.

00:24:04.030 --> 00:24:06.030
- What did you say? - That we have 58,000 of yours...

00:24:06.030 --> 00:24:08.950
- Permit me, you can't talk like that. - Of course.

00:24:08.950 --> 00:24:11.840
I can't talk like that as a saleswoman, but she can insult me as a star, right?

00:24:11.840 --> 00:24:13.840
All this is a misunderstanding that we are going to explain to you.

00:24:13.840 --> 00:24:17.840
All this is a scene of disgust of which you are to blame, and you have the obligation to defend me.

00:24:17.840 --> 00:24:20.850
- We are going to... - What? Are you going to defend her again?

00:24:20.850 --> 00:24:22.850
Calm down, please, calm down!

00:24:22.850 --> 00:24:24.850
We are not trying to defend anyone, but to make us understand each other.

00:24:24.850 --> 00:24:27.850
- Oh, then get along with my father. - But calm down!

00:24:27.850 --> 00:24:30.000
- Excuse me. Don't worry, we have to go. - Come on.

00:24:32.970 --> 00:24:35.530
- We're sorry. - I'm the one who's sorry.

00:24:35.680 --> 00:24:37.990
Anyway, thank you for the recording.

00:24:38.950 --> 00:24:43.670
- Good night. - Sorry, I had my hands busy.

00:24:43.750 --> 00:24:45.710
- And now what? - The news.

00:24:45.790 --> 00:24:49.170
The lawyer of the Paris doll has filed a lawsuit against him.

00:24:49.250 --> 00:24:50.900
What do we do?

00:24:50.980 --> 00:24:54.440
- So, it's not a problem anymore. - Tell me, as a manager, what do you advise?

00:24:54.520 --> 00:24:57.830
From an economic point of view, there are two solutions.

00:24:57.910 --> 00:25:00.000
- Which ones? - We send you to kill the lawyer...

00:25:00.060 --> 00:25:03.080
Or do we kill each other?

00:25:05.810 --> 00:25:08.880
Well, I'll leave you to think about it, gentlemen.

00:25:08.960 --> 00:25:11.460
But, beware, the tide is rising.

00:25:12.540 --> 00:25:19.880
- Up to here. - Good morning.

00:25:21.280 --> 00:25:22.390
Good morning, Mr. Vulcano.

00:25:22.470 --> 00:25:24.130
I've gathered you to tell you that,

00:25:24.210 --> 00:25:26.500
in honor of the relevant conditions,

00:25:26.670 --> 00:25:30.000
the dedication and the faith placed in the destinies of the company,

00:25:30.800 --> 00:25:34.580
The Vulcano & Co. directorate has decided unanimously

00:25:35.080 --> 00:25:37.400
to appoint the head of the sales department

00:25:38.770 --> 00:25:40.850
Ms. Isabel de Castro.

00:25:49.340 --> 00:25:56.170
That's all.

00:25:56.260 --> 00:26:00.000
You may leave, except for Ms. Isabel de Castro.

00:26:04.190 --> 00:26:17.690
- Just go. - The new head of sales.

00:26:19.610 --> 00:26:21.760
Simply brilliant.

00:26:22.560 --> 00:26:25.960
Ladies, congratulations. Yesterday saleswoman, today head of sales.

00:26:26.160 --> 00:26:28.930
Who says she'll be a partner of the firm tomorrow?

00:26:30.120 --> 00:26:33.020
- I don't know what to say. - It doesn't matter. He'll say it all.

00:26:33.020 --> 00:26:37.070
- All what? - All we've talked about in our plans for the future.

00:26:37.070 --> 00:26:42.890
The canoe, the water problem, those 20 million things we have in our hands.

00:26:42.890 --> 00:26:44.060
Excuse me.

00:26:44.060 --> 00:26:49.910
- Do you have problems with water, sir? - Yes.

00:26:49.910 --> 00:26:52.960
No, no. Well, we'll see about that later, right?

00:26:52.960 --> 00:26:57.550
What do you think if we have lunch together?

00:26:57.550 --> 00:27:00.000
Of course, sir. I always have lunch with my wife.

00:27:00.060 --> 00:27:01.860
with my friend at the restaurant in La Huerta.

00:27:01.860 --> 00:27:02.820
I'd love to.

00:27:02.820 --> 00:27:08.030
I need to talk to you in peace, in a quiet place.

00:27:09.910 --> 00:27:11.910
Excuse me, sir.

00:27:14.970 --> 00:27:17.970
- Give me a black chorizo. - They're colored.

00:27:17.970 --> 00:27:19.970
- A black chorizo. - Yes, ma'am.

00:27:19.970 --> 00:27:22.800
- And your blanket? - I don't have it.

00:27:22.800 --> 00:27:25.800
- He wants to pick you up in the back. - In the back?

00:27:25.800 --> 00:27:27.800
- Wait, I'll be right back. - Of course, ma'am.

00:27:27.800 --> 00:27:29.920
Excuse me. Excuse me.

00:27:30.160 --> 00:27:38.890
Look, he's lost. He's going to look for the covers.

00:27:39.870 --> 00:27:40.870
But it's a good deal, isn't it?

00:27:41.870 --> 00:27:43.870
Yes, but I don't understand this about the elevator, you know?

00:27:45.870 --> 00:27:47.610
They must have wanted to fix it last night.

00:27:48.610 --> 00:27:49.440
Possibly.

00:27:50.390 --> 00:27:52.330
A car of good quality, sir. The price is modest.

00:27:53.330 --> 00:27:54.330
No, no, not today. Just a couple of halfs.

00:27:55.330 --> 00:27:56.340
I have halfs, thank you.

00:27:57.340 --> 00:27:58.340
No, nothing, thank you, thank you.

00:28:01.310 --> 00:28:04.840
- Now I know. - What? You want a glass?

00:28:04.840 --> 00:28:07.690
- No, I don't need a glass. - No, sir, no, no.

00:28:07.690 --> 00:28:10.190
You have to look for it there, where it says "glass".

00:28:10.190 --> 00:28:14.190
Oh, yes? I just passed by, I didn't notice. I'll be right back.

00:28:14.190 --> 00:28:18.580
- They didn't tell you anything about the test? - No.

00:28:18.580 --> 00:28:22.030
- And why don't you ask me? - I don't dare.

00:28:22.030 --> 00:28:24.170
It must have been similar or scary.

00:28:24.170 --> 00:28:27.060
I'm sorry, sir, I don't have any interest in this fruit sundae.

00:28:27.060 --> 00:28:30.000
I asked for it for my wife and I couldn't find it.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:31.600
- If you don't want it. - Well, let's go.

00:28:31.800 --> 00:28:33.490
- Two 6.50. - Oh, yes.

00:28:33.690 --> 00:28:35.090
- Get in, please. - Yes, excuse me, sir.

00:28:35.290 --> 00:28:36.690
- It's yours, here. - Excuse me.

00:28:36.890 --> 00:28:38.690
- This is yours, sir. - Yes.

00:28:38.890 --> 00:28:40.890
- Just take the ticket. - Thank you very much.

00:28:41.690 --> 00:28:43.890
- Well, now yes. - Well.

00:28:44.090 --> 00:28:45.490
- Where are you going? - To work, sir.

00:28:45.690 --> 00:28:46.890
There are three minutes left for the hour.

00:28:47.090 --> 00:28:49.690
If we didn't go to this place, it's so practical, we wouldn't have time to eat.

00:28:49.890 --> 00:28:52.690
Oh, don't worry. I'll give you permission to arrive half an hour later.

00:28:52.890 --> 00:28:54.890
Oh, no, sir. Thank you very much, but it's impossible.

00:28:55.090 --> 00:28:56.690
A gesture must set the example.

00:28:56.890 --> 00:28:58.890
- See you later, sir. - See you later, sir.

00:28:59.090 --> 00:28:59.920
See you later.

00:29:01.560 --> 00:29:04.080
What a beautiful business!

00:29:04.080 --> 00:29:11.220
The owners, who are charming, have appointed me as the sales manager.

00:29:11.220 --> 00:29:22.470
With the increase, I will be able to save a little more to fulfill my two hopes.

00:29:38.380 --> 00:29:42.080
I'm so proud that these days, the town's patron's party is celebrated.

00:29:42.790 --> 00:29:46.390
I'd give all the air I can breathe to be there with you,

00:29:46.620 --> 00:29:47.840
at the happy parties,

00:29:48.040 --> 00:29:52.690
having fun between the roses, the algarabía and the songs,

00:29:53.170 --> 00:29:56.240
the first ones you taught me, my little mother,

00:29:56.460 --> 00:29:57.970
and that I've learned since I was little.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:04.680
- Long live Cádiz! - Long live our country!

00:30:30.350 --> 00:30:36.240
-

00:31:30.670 --> 00:31:35.370
Oh, my God.

00:31:35.370 --> 00:31:50.200
Oh, my God.

00:33:17.850 --> 00:33:23.040
Kiss with all your heart your daughter, who loves you more than me.

00:33:37.360 --> 00:33:39.430
- Thank you, boss. - Boss, ma'am?

00:33:39.630 --> 00:33:41.870
Isabel, will you sign the ticket?

00:33:42.070 --> 00:33:48.400
Boss, ma'am?

00:33:49.020 --> 00:33:50.220
Boss, ma'am?

00:33:50.600 --> 00:33:53.550
I've listened to all the records. There's no scratch.

00:33:53.680 --> 00:33:55.940
Very well. I have another job for you.

00:33:56.140 --> 00:33:57.080
- Another one? - Uh-huh.

00:33:57.280 --> 00:34:00.000
Take out the green covers from the classic records.

00:34:00.160 --> 00:34:02.180
And you change them for the yellow ones from the Reya.

00:34:02.180 --> 00:34:05.750
The light blue ones from the Folklorica, for the lilac ones with black bands from the Brazilians.

00:34:05.750 --> 00:34:08.480
And the red colors from the Superestas, for the brown ones from the Zarzuelas.

00:34:08.480 --> 00:34:10.770
- Is that clear? - Yes, ma'am.

00:34:10.770 --> 00:34:14.370
- Let me know when you're done, I have work to do. - Excuse me, ma'am.

00:34:14.370 --> 00:34:16.170
- The address. - Thank you.

00:34:16.170 --> 00:34:18.850
- Excuse me, ma'am. - Go on.

00:34:18.850 --> 00:34:19.910
Yes, ma'am.

00:34:19.910 --> 00:34:29.920
Miss Isabel.

00:34:30.540 --> 00:34:35.530
I've been wanting to talk to you in a quiet place for a long time,

00:34:35.880 --> 00:34:38.960
because I have to confess something that may seem unusual to you,

00:34:39.700 --> 00:34:41.950
but that I can't keep quiet about.

00:34:42.150 --> 00:34:46.100
Isabel. Excuse me.

00:34:46.930 --> 00:34:50.990
Yes? No, I can't answer.

00:34:51.620 --> 00:34:56.560
Well, I'm busy. Well, tell me, but quickly.

00:35:00.250 --> 00:35:03.050
- What's wrong? - We need her for a meeting.

00:35:03.050 --> 00:35:05.910
Good. Low, huh?

00:35:05.910 --> 00:35:08.890
- Miss, you can go up. - Okay, miss.

00:35:08.890 --> 00:35:10.250
Okay, fine.

00:35:10.250 --> 00:35:16.070
Talk to Mr. Gerardo.

00:35:16.070 --> 00:35:21.420
Miss Isabel, you've asked yourself a lot of questions since yesterday, haven't you?

00:35:21.420 --> 00:35:22.700
I'm going to answer them.

00:35:22.700 --> 00:35:24.300
Alvicias!

00:35:24.300 --> 00:35:27.580
Sister Menendez has just joined you.

00:35:27.580 --> 00:35:29.570
- And they want to talk to you. - But I'm not here.

00:35:30.120 --> 00:35:32.540
You know I'm not here. Talk to Gerardo.

00:35:32.880 --> 00:35:35.140
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:35:35.140 --> 00:35:37.440
No, Gerardo isn't here. No, the one who is is you. I saw him.

00:35:37.440 --> 00:35:39.940
But I don't want to attend. I can't attend because I have a headache

00:35:39.940 --> 00:35:43.820
and I don't want to come in here. Please, please, please!

00:35:43.820 --> 00:35:49.780
- Yes, but he's here, right? - But please!

00:35:49.780 --> 00:35:54.030
Isabel, I...

00:35:54.030 --> 00:35:57.090
- Excuse me. - Yes, of course.

00:35:57.090 --> 00:35:58.960
- Let's see if they're correct. - Let's see.

00:36:03.870 --> 00:36:05.670
It's the new layout of the shelves.

00:36:05.710 --> 00:36:07.110
I'm reorganizing the section.

00:36:07.150 --> 00:36:08.950
It's very nice, eh? Very nice, especially the bar.

00:36:08.990 --> 00:36:10.670
No, no, no, I don't like it.

00:36:10.710 --> 00:36:12.470
- Who did this? - The artist, miss.

00:36:12.510 --> 00:36:14.470
- Call him from the inside, please. - No, no, no.

00:36:14.570 --> 00:36:17.520
- What were you going to tell me, sir? - Sit down, please.

00:36:17.560 --> 00:36:19.030
Yes, sir. Thank you.

00:36:19.140 --> 00:36:22.630
Isabel, I wanted to tell you that...

00:36:23.300 --> 00:36:26.300
- Excuse me. - What do you want?

00:36:26.340 --> 00:36:28.720
What? News of the last moment.

00:36:28.750 --> 00:36:30.000
Sister Menendez...

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:33.000
They don't want to talk to Gerardo. They insist on seeing you to the force.

00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:35.000
To the force? Call the police.

00:36:35.000 --> 00:36:37.000
It's not necessary, they already went to call them.

00:36:37.000 --> 00:36:39.110
May I, Mr. Manager?

00:36:39.110 --> 00:36:43.110
Look, I need the cost list of the records to start a sale of liquidation. Can I?

00:36:43.110 --> 00:36:46.110
But wonderful, wonderful, colossal!

00:36:46.110 --> 00:36:48.110
- I'll bring it right away. - Thank you very much.

00:36:48.110 --> 00:36:50.830
- Well, look, I wanted to explain... - May I?

00:36:50.830 --> 00:36:52.830
- Did you call me? - Yes, yes.

00:36:52.830 --> 00:36:54.830
- Sorry, Mr. Burcano. - Just go.

00:36:54.830 --> 00:36:56.830
Listen, this has nothing to do with what I asked you.

00:36:56.830 --> 00:37:00.000
Oh, no, no, no, no. But there's a mistake here.

00:37:01.790 --> 00:37:04.830
You explain it to her, I'll be right back.

00:37:04.830 --> 00:37:07.420
Excuse me.

00:37:07.420 --> 00:37:10.170
- What's going on? - I'm sorry, ma'am.

00:37:10.170 --> 00:37:11.650
Fine, sign the ticket.

00:37:11.650 --> 00:37:13.670
It's something very difficult.

00:37:13.670 --> 00:37:16.370
Fine, tell her to go up.

00:37:16.370 --> 00:37:18.730
- Fine, go up then, please. - Fine.

00:37:18.730 --> 00:37:21.780
- Look, I wanted to explain, I don't want to... - Miss Isabel!

00:37:21.780 --> 00:37:26.280
- The costs... - This column or this one?

00:37:26.280 --> 00:37:28.730
Neither this column nor this one, I'll explain it to her.

00:37:28.730 --> 00:37:30.000
Ma'am, what are you doing?

00:37:30.860 --> 00:37:33.180
- Excuse me. - Come in, come in.

00:37:34.360 --> 00:37:36.100
- Yes? - I'm done with the covers.

00:37:36.140 --> 00:37:38.120
- I have another job for you. - Yes, ma'am.

00:37:38.140 --> 00:37:40.400
Look, 5,000 scarabs arrived in rubber.

00:37:40.420 --> 00:37:42.900
You stick them one by one on the folkloric records.

00:37:42.920 --> 00:37:43.560
- Yes. - Understood?

00:37:43.580 --> 00:37:45.380
- Yes, the... - Yes, one by one.

00:37:46.170 --> 00:37:47.950
- In rubber, yes, yes. - Yes, ma'am.

00:37:47.970 --> 00:37:49.830
- Yes, go ahead. - Let's see.

00:37:49.850 --> 00:37:52.100
Ma'am, there's a big problem here.

00:37:52.120 --> 00:37:53.750
Is it a return?

00:37:53.770 --> 00:37:54.790
Yes and no.

00:37:54.810 --> 00:37:58.740
I want to return this part of the record, but keep the other one.

00:38:00.540 --> 00:38:04.700
Let's see. I'm going to explain it to you, let's see.

00:38:06.470 --> 00:38:29.800
- Thinking. - Silently.

00:38:31.150 --> 00:38:33.150
Now no one will be able to stop you from listening to me.

00:38:33.330 --> 00:38:36.070
It's been five days since I've looked for a way to talk to you in a serene way.

00:38:36.170 --> 00:38:40.470
In a quiet place, about something that I've been wanting to confess to you for a long time.

00:38:40.680 --> 00:38:43.000
Shouldn't you have forced me to quit my job?

00:38:43.110 --> 00:38:44.830
- Is it so important? - Yes.

00:38:44.930 --> 00:38:48.160
But you see, I don't know how to start.

00:38:48.300 --> 00:38:51.160
- You start at the beginning. - It'll be the best.

00:38:51.410 --> 00:38:56.090
Miss Isabel, I'm madly in love with you.

00:38:56.580 --> 00:39:00.000
- Sir... - No, no, no.

00:39:00.800 --> 00:39:02.630
Don't tell me anything, don't embarrass me.

00:39:03.560 --> 00:39:05.260
I don't know how to invent beautiful phrases.

00:39:05.710 --> 00:39:08.210
That's why I have to say it like this, savagely.

00:39:08.870 --> 00:39:11.170
Like this uncontainable love that was born in me.

00:39:11.490 --> 00:39:12.990
But sir, what about me?

00:39:13.190 --> 00:39:14.700
No, no, no, don't talk to me.

00:39:15.280 --> 00:39:18.740
I beg you, I don't know how hard it was for me to decide.

00:39:19.280 --> 00:39:23.190
I've always been shy with women, and it's the first time I fall in love.

00:39:24.220 --> 00:39:27.230
Imagine what I suffered in silence, spying on her every day.

00:39:27.630 --> 00:39:30.000
Overwhelmingly affectionate. You don't believe me, do you?

00:39:30.670 --> 00:39:32.700
Speak to me, Isabel. Tell me something.

00:39:32.700 --> 00:39:34.310
Forget the differences of classes.

00:39:34.310 --> 00:39:37.270
Don't think that I'm a rich man and you're a modest maid.

00:39:37.270 --> 00:39:40.340
If you were rich and I was poor, I wouldn't care.

00:39:40.340 --> 00:39:42.250
Be as democratic as I am.

00:39:42.250 --> 00:39:43.700
Speak to me, Isabel.

00:39:43.700 --> 00:39:45.900
I don't know, sir. I didn't expect all this.

00:39:45.900 --> 00:39:49.180
Don't look at me as a man. Look at the illusion.

00:39:49.180 --> 00:39:51.270
My illusion is different, sir.

00:39:51.270 --> 00:39:53.300
All my dreams are in my career.

00:39:53.300 --> 00:39:54.840
Singing is my greatest ambition.

00:39:54.840 --> 00:39:56.850
Until I succeed, I can't think of anything else.

00:39:56.850 --> 00:39:58.090
You have to think of love.

00:39:58.090 --> 00:40:00.000
Love will help you succeed.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:02.600
I'll help you. Vulcano and company are going to help you.

00:40:02.600 --> 00:40:04.900
Think about the desperation I'm talking to you about.

00:40:04.900 --> 00:40:07.220
Answer me, Isabel!

00:40:07.220 --> 00:40:08.820
Don't ask me that, for God's sake!

00:40:08.820 --> 00:40:11.220
If you don't answer me, I'll feel sinking.

00:40:11.220 --> 00:40:17.440
And with me, my hopes, my joys, the Vulcano house, everything will sink.

00:40:17.440 --> 00:40:19.240
But you can't force me to do this!

00:40:19.240 --> 00:40:23.430
I'll give you a minute. Either you answer me, or I'll throw myself into the water!

00:40:23.430 --> 00:40:24.990
We're sinking!

00:40:24.990 --> 00:40:27.440
The Juas manufacturers just sent us the embargo.

00:40:27.440 --> 00:40:30.000
Luckily, I just spoke to the Justice Officer, and...

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:31.800
I got ample facilities for the payment.

00:40:31.800 --> 00:40:33.400
- Really? - Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes.

00:40:33.400 --> 00:40:37.200
We have to pay half right now and the other half tomorrow at the first hour.

00:40:37.200 --> 00:40:39.820
The water doesn't dry up here.

00:40:40.660 --> 00:40:41.860
What do you answer me now?

00:40:41.860 --> 00:40:44.760
I'm sorry, but until I succeed, I won't be able to think about love.

00:40:44.760 --> 00:40:45.480
Really?

00:40:45.480 --> 00:40:46.580
You loved him.

00:40:46.580 --> 00:40:47.580
No!

00:40:47.580 --> 00:40:48.580
Oh, no!

00:40:48.580 --> 00:40:50.680
Mr. Volcano! Mr. Volcano!

00:40:50.680 --> 00:40:58.180
Mr. Volcano!

00:40:58.180 --> 00:40:59.180
Cheers.

00:41:01.240 --> 00:41:02.960
More than I made it impossible.

00:41:02.960 --> 00:41:06.280
Until he succeeds in his career, he doesn't even want to think about love.

00:41:06.280 --> 00:41:08.360
- And well, you have to make him succeed. - It's very easy.

00:41:08.360 --> 00:41:10.530
- Did you hear him sing? - I didn't.

00:41:10.530 --> 00:41:11.830
But that's the least.

00:41:11.830 --> 00:41:14.600
A triumph is almost always the product of imagination.

00:41:14.600 --> 00:41:16.520
Suggestion. That's the word.

00:41:16.520 --> 00:41:19.590
A triumph is organized, invented, manufactured.

00:41:19.590 --> 00:41:21.130
Think about it. See you tomorrow.

00:41:21.130 --> 00:41:25.870
- Forty. Bring me another blanket. - Well.

00:41:25.870 --> 00:41:27.980
Extraordinary, artistic concourse.

00:41:27.980 --> 00:41:30.000
Volcan and company are looking for work.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:33.960
- What do you think? - I think this contest...

00:41:33.960 --> 00:41:36.800
- ...will have to be done in a submarine. - Why?

00:41:36.800 --> 00:41:39.340
Because the water, gentlemen, will get us here.

00:41:39.340 --> 00:41:42.100
You're wrong, Mr. Salvador. This contest is our salvation.

00:41:42.100 --> 00:41:44.980
We stop the jury, the jury names her, and she looks for him.

00:41:44.980 --> 00:41:45.980
- Who? - Me.

00:41:45.980 --> 00:41:47.980
Because he already looked for her.

00:41:47.980 --> 00:41:49.980
- Who is she? - The winner of the contest.

00:41:49.980 --> 00:41:52.030
But how are they going to look for her if they don't know who she is?

00:41:52.030 --> 00:41:54.030
Yes, we know. She's the one who's going to choose the jury.

00:41:54.030 --> 00:41:56.040
But how do you know who the jury is going to choose?

00:41:56.040 --> 00:41:58.040
There it is. Because the jury is going to choose the one...

00:41:58.040 --> 00:42:00.000
...who is the winner of the contest.

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:02.800
And the singer too. God bless her.

00:42:02.800 --> 00:42:07.600
She, he, the juror, the sailor, they're all going to drown!

00:42:07.600 --> 00:42:10.200
I'm going to drown!

00:42:10.200 --> 00:42:13.230
Television receives with great enthusiasm

00:42:13.230 --> 00:42:17.430
this magnificent opportunity that the Vulcano House and Company

00:42:17.430 --> 00:42:19.630
offers to all young people.

00:42:19.630 --> 00:42:23.970
The youthful voice of the song is sought.

00:42:42.730 --> 00:42:44.690
I don't think so, right, Dad?

00:42:44.730 --> 00:42:47.530
I've always said that all contests are...

00:42:47.570 --> 00:42:50.330
Well, like all jurors, they're sold out.

00:42:50.370 --> 00:42:52.880
So what's going on? That's why I don't...

00:42:52.920 --> 00:42:54.880
You have a lot of reason, Do Jeremia.

00:42:54.920 --> 00:42:56.920
Why? Don't you want to sign up?

00:42:56.960 --> 00:43:00.000
Me? No, I've always wanted to sign up.

00:43:00.600 --> 00:43:03.500
- This is my opinion. I'll explain it to you. - No, I'll do it myself.

00:43:03.600 --> 00:43:10.860
Mr. Vulcano, what a surprise!

00:43:10.960 --> 00:43:12.860
- Come in. - Excuse me.

00:43:12.960 --> 00:43:16.190
- Come in. - For you.

00:43:16.290 --> 00:43:23.410
- You know my parents, don't you? - Yes, I have to talk to you.

00:43:23.510 --> 00:43:26.410
- Then we'll leave you alone. - No, it's not necessary.

00:43:26.510 --> 00:43:29.570
Besides, I also have to talk to you.

00:43:30.190 --> 00:43:34.450
- I'm sorry, Mr. Vesuvius. - Burcano, ma'am. Mario Burcano.

00:43:34.550 --> 00:43:37.390
- Sit down, sit down. - Sit down, sit down.

00:43:37.760 --> 00:43:42.830
Dear teacher, the Burcano & Co. House has studied its musical antecedents

00:43:42.930 --> 00:43:45.330
and, on account of its relevant conditions,

00:43:45.430 --> 00:43:47.590
wants to request, through me,

00:43:47.690 --> 00:43:51.370
the honor of appointing the jury for our competition.

00:43:51.470 --> 00:43:55.450
I think that the jury, that the jury...

00:43:55.550 --> 00:44:00.000
That's why this determination by the House, of the House,

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:03.040
and company have chosen very well.

00:44:03.040 --> 00:44:03.920
Accept, accept.

00:44:03.920 --> 00:44:07.260
The name of the signature I represent, thank you very much.

00:44:07.260 --> 00:44:10.060
This has to be celebrated, Susana, serve Jerez the signature.

00:44:10.060 --> 00:44:11.060
Of course, dad.

00:44:11.060 --> 00:44:15.440
As for you, Miss Isabel, I want to ask you in the presence of all, something that

00:44:15.440 --> 00:44:18.400
can depend on your happiness and also mine.

00:44:18.400 --> 00:44:19.400
No!

00:44:19.400 --> 00:44:24.320
I mean, it's not appropriate, we've already talked about that.

00:44:24.320 --> 00:44:30.000
That was in bottled water, I want to make a request to Secas.

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:33.770
- Tomorrow at the store? - No, today and here.

00:44:33.770 --> 00:44:38.720
Better in the yard, it's cooler. I'll tell you later.

00:44:38.720 --> 00:44:43.080
Mr. Volcano, why do you insist?

00:44:43.080 --> 00:44:45.880
I already told you that until I succeed in my career, I can't talk about anything else.

00:44:45.880 --> 00:44:49.880
Precisely, I'm here to give you the opportunity. Sign up for the contest.

00:44:49.880 --> 00:44:53.140
Oh, that's something else.

00:44:53.140 --> 00:44:57.580
- But sir, the contests are all fraud. - Oh, no, huh? Not this one.

00:44:57.580 --> 00:45:00.000
You can't think badly of the Volcanoes.

00:45:00.030 --> 00:45:06.280
- Where were you going, Isabel? - Sorry, but I work in your house and people are going to live there.

00:45:06.280 --> 00:45:11.560
Be careful, I'll take care of that too. You won't be the house's employee for the jury. What do you say?

00:45:11.560 --> 00:45:17.960
- God will say so. - Isabel, I...

00:45:17.960 --> 00:45:28.930
I gave you my whole soul in an image of your arms

00:45:31.400 --> 00:45:35.620
For you, I was a simple vixen

00:45:35.730 --> 00:45:40.020
Who breaks with a betrayal

00:45:41.660 --> 00:45:48.470
I want to follow you, I want to shut up

00:45:48.670 --> 00:45:53.010
This love is better than suffering

00:45:53.210 --> 00:45:58.290
Having to die, rip me apart at once

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:00.610
- Good luck.

00:46:31.400 --> 00:46:33.400
and you killed my illusions

00:46:33.400 --> 00:46:52.910
thank you very much

00:46:52.910 --> 00:46:54.910
you are so good

00:46:54.910 --> 00:46:56.920
virgin of the macarena

00:46:56.920 --> 00:46:58.920
take away the pity

00:46:58.920 --> 00:47:00.000
of loving without loving me

00:47:00.890 --> 00:47:21.440
I'm going to take a little bit of rose water from her who drinks cold.

00:47:30.440 --> 00:47:45.480
Selected. Eliminated!

00:47:45.480 --> 00:47:56.770
Eliminated!

00:47:56.770 --> 00:47:58.800
Miss Isabel de Castro,

00:48:30.700 --> 00:48:34.200
For Christ's sake, don't break any more, miss.

00:48:34.300 --> 00:48:35.380
I beg you.

00:48:35.480 --> 00:48:38.680
Oh, what are you doing, my God, you're going to kill me.

00:48:38.780 --> 00:48:42.540
- My dear, my dear, my treasure. - So, instead of...

00:48:42.640 --> 00:48:45.080
...fulfilling the contracts, you organize contests.

00:48:45.180 --> 00:48:47.290
- No, dear, I'm going to explain it to you. - Don't explain it to me.

00:48:47.390 --> 00:48:49.790
- It's a commercial maneuver, isn't it, Gerardo? - Yes, of course.

00:48:49.890 --> 00:48:52.890
- What we ask of you is a little patience, and in that way... - Patience, patience.

00:48:52.990 --> 00:48:54.810
- Be nice, be nice. - I always ask for patience.

00:48:54.910 --> 00:48:58.470
- Be nice, please, please, we ask for it. - I can't, I can't.

00:48:58.570 --> 00:49:00.000
- Thank you very much. - You're welcome.

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:04.500
- We were waiting for you. - Do the best you can to ruin the contest.

00:49:04.700 --> 00:49:07.460
- And this ruins it, huh? - How can I not pay?

00:49:08.390 --> 00:49:11.530
Ladies and gentlemen, in a few moments,

00:49:11.730 --> 00:49:16.450
the sensational contest of the Vulcan House and Company will begin

00:49:16.810 --> 00:49:20.850
to choose among the finalists the youthful voice of the song.

00:49:21.050 --> 00:49:23.940
We are waiting for the judge's decision.

00:49:25.120 --> 00:49:30.000
Voice.

00:49:30.640 --> 00:49:32.940
- There are only one juror left. - But why?

00:49:33.040 --> 00:49:35.240
The Justice Department has received a complaint

00:49:35.340 --> 00:49:38.440
and is obliged to intervene by changing the members that compose it

00:49:38.540 --> 00:49:40.840
to ensure the unanimity of the contest.

00:49:40.940 --> 00:49:42.710
- A complaint? - No, no.

00:49:42.720 --> 00:49:44.390
- But you can't do that. - Of course.

00:49:44.490 --> 00:49:46.690
Where are we going to get another juror at this hour?

00:49:46.790 --> 00:49:49.490
Don't worry, everything is planned.

00:49:49.560 --> 00:49:51.120
Look.

00:49:53.060 --> 00:49:56.460
The waltz of happy memories

00:49:56.560 --> 00:50:00.000
That we danced, you and I, this night of love

00:50:00.960 --> 00:50:07.920
What did you say? "My soul, I love you."

00:50:07.920 --> 00:50:14.850
We lost love, because life gave us other paths.

00:50:14.850 --> 00:50:22.090
Until that waltz, he left, he stayed, and it's his song that took us up to the skies.

00:50:22.090 --> 00:50:24.640
I like it, I like it.

00:50:24.640 --> 00:50:27.550
Either you convince yourself of Pinocanti, or we do the "Papelón del Sigmo".

00:50:27.550 --> 00:50:30.000
I prefer the "Papelón" to disillusion her, what are you saying?

00:50:30.030 --> 00:50:33.030
She sings "goodbye triumph", "goodbye romance", and "goodbye PC".

00:50:33.030 --> 00:50:36.030
And I can convince you. I've done enough, haven't I?

00:50:37.970 --> 00:50:40.770
I'm going to convince her.

00:50:45.150 --> 00:50:48.150
What you've done with the jury is...

00:50:49.150 --> 00:50:52.110
And since that means there isn't any...

00:50:52.110 --> 00:50:54.110
Therefore, you have to...

00:50:54.110 --> 00:50:59.120
I want to prove that with or without you, I have enough merit to deserve the triumph.

00:50:59.120 --> 00:51:00.000
Don't you think so?

00:51:00.060 --> 00:51:06.730
- Go ahead. It's my turn. - No, I need to talk to you alone.

00:51:06.850 --> 00:51:11.480
- Please, Mr. Jeremia. - Oh, come on, they'll kick me out today.

00:51:12.640 --> 00:51:19.520
- Miss Isabel, you can't sing. - What?

00:51:19.640 --> 00:51:22.380
- You can't sing. - I don't understand, Mr. Vulcano.

00:51:22.500 --> 00:51:24.940
Well, it's better to say, you shouldn't sing.

00:51:25.060 --> 00:51:28.170
What happened to the priest doesn't offer any security.

00:51:28.290 --> 00:51:30.000
Oh, but I have a lot of faith.

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:34.580
But I don't. I mean, I don't have faith in the jury.

00:51:34.610 --> 00:51:37.810
- Imagine if I don't win. - I'd be very disappointed.

00:51:37.890 --> 00:51:41.060
- You would? - But I'll start again.

00:51:41.080 --> 00:51:44.670
My dream is to win. Only when that happens, I'll start living.

00:51:44.750 --> 00:51:47.350
So you mean to say that despite the jury against you?

00:51:47.380 --> 00:51:51.220
- I'll do the same. - In that case, Miss Isabel,

00:51:51.220 --> 00:51:54.230
- I must confess something to you. - Isabel!

00:51:54.260 --> 00:51:56.560
- They're calling you! - Yes, yes.

00:52:00.730 --> 00:52:02.930
What did you want to tell me, Mr. Burcano?

00:52:03.200 --> 00:52:07.770
My wish. My wish is that your wish will come true.

00:52:18.960 --> 00:52:30.000
- He spoke to you? And he didn't say anything? - Yes, Mr. Burcano.

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:35.060
- Thank you very much. - The last finalist, Miss Isabel de Castro.

00:52:35.360 --> 00:52:36.860
- Excuse me. - Yes.

00:53:00.060 --> 00:53:03.220
murciana de la hermosura

00:53:03.220 --> 00:53:06.050
Novia vestida de flor de azahar

00:53:06.050 --> 00:53:12.040
Entre en naranjo el seguro de su barraca

00:53:12.040 --> 00:53:14.820
Copia al pasar

00:53:14.820 --> 00:53:18.500
A la puerta de Murcia tus aguas cantan

00:53:18.500 --> 00:53:22.210
Por mil acequias con graves olas

00:53:22.210 --> 00:53:25.190
Son de guitarra rosita

00:53:30.510 --> 00:53:33.510
"with a beautiful heart."

00:53:33.710 --> 00:53:38.510
"My little garden has purple eyes."

00:53:38.640 --> 00:53:48.650
"My little garden has purple eyes."

00:53:48.850 --> 00:53:53.080
"I steal your eyes, my little little strength."

00:54:09.310 --> 00:54:11.680
- You have a bitter smile. - No.

00:54:30.440 --> 00:54:34.400
Divine land, grace and love

00:54:34.400 --> 00:54:37.810
The beauty of your women

00:54:37.810 --> 00:54:42.680
Made of nacre, silk and sun

00:55:04.670 --> 00:55:06.390
It seems that you like it.

00:55:06.390 --> 00:55:09.060
Yes, yes.

00:55:09.060 --> 00:55:12.690
♫ It's the beauty of your women. ♫

00:55:12.690 --> 00:55:22.730
♫ Made of nacre, silk and salt. ♫

00:55:22.730 --> 00:55:26.820
♫ Inside of them. ♫

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:05.710
for unanimity to Isabel de Castro as the youthful voice of the song.

00:56:08.590 --> 00:56:13.110
Let's toast to Isabel de Castro, our sensational discovery.

00:56:13.910 --> 00:56:20.770
- Shall we dance, gentlemen? - Of course.

00:56:34.250 --> 00:56:37.750
Isabel, isn't this where I would have wanted to tell you that I am?

00:56:37.750 --> 00:56:41.530
Yes, I know. You need a quiet place to talk to me serenely.

00:56:41.530 --> 00:56:44.920
Don't make fun of me, Isabel, and especially now that the great moment has come.

00:56:44.920 --> 00:56:48.470
You have to fulfill your promise of listening to my desperate love.

00:56:48.470 --> 00:56:51.570
I finally achieved your dream. You triumphed.

00:56:51.570 --> 00:56:56.420
Don't exaggerate, Mr. Buscano. This is nothing more than the first step in your dream.

00:56:56.420 --> 00:56:59.670
Nothing more? But what kind of ladder is the triumph for you?

00:57:00.060 --> 00:57:04.290
I imagine her very tall, with all colors of hair.

00:57:04.340 --> 00:57:07.090
And in the last one, the birth of a slide

00:57:07.180 --> 00:57:10.320
that delights life, or love, perhaps.

00:57:10.560 --> 00:57:12.650
To succeed. To succeed.

00:57:13.030 --> 00:57:14.870
It seems she doesn't care about anything else.

00:57:15.010 --> 00:57:17.030
- What happens is that you don't care. - Me?

00:57:17.170 --> 00:57:19.850
Please. It's all a hair problem.

00:57:19.910 --> 00:57:22.500
She wants a ladder. Well, I'll get her a ladder.

00:57:22.700 --> 00:57:24.440
Big news!

00:57:24.530 --> 00:57:27.280
The money from the box was just enough

00:57:27.480 --> 00:57:28.940
to seal the contract with Isabel Descartes.

00:57:29.140 --> 00:57:30.000
Leave the contract.

00:57:30.510 --> 00:57:32.050
How? The first time we have something good?

00:57:32.050 --> 00:57:33.690
No, no, no, no, we have to record with her, huh?

00:57:33.690 --> 00:57:34.940
That's not enough.

00:57:34.940 --> 00:57:36.910
What we have to do is something else.

00:57:36.910 --> 00:57:38.690
We will clean the city with her name.

00:57:38.690 --> 00:57:41.790
We will make Isabel de Castro the sensation, the idol, the great figure.

00:57:41.790 --> 00:57:43.510
We will not stop until she becomes famous.

00:57:43.510 --> 00:57:44.710
And all that with what?

00:57:44.710 --> 00:57:47.670
With promises, with documents, with futuristic papers, with illusions,

00:57:47.670 --> 00:57:49.950
on account of the inheritance of 20 million pesetas.

00:57:49.950 --> 00:57:51.870
Go, go, go, go, go, stop joking, man.

00:57:51.870 --> 00:57:53.790
The Crescente has tragic characteristics.

00:57:53.790 --> 00:57:54.880
They are not jokes.

00:57:54.880 --> 00:57:57.770
Isabel de Castro is the heir of 20 million pesetas.

00:57:57.770 --> 00:57:58.370
Is it true?

00:57:58.370 --> 00:58:00.000
So how not to help her

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:02.720
- You'll be the last one to go. - Come on, come on!

00:58:02.920 --> 00:58:05.520
The water can climb stairs.

00:58:05.720 --> 00:58:09.000
- Does she know about inheritance? - No, she's funny, huh?

00:58:09.200 --> 00:58:11.560
Before she knows, she'll be the most ruttinant in the country.

00:58:11.760 --> 00:58:15.250
She'll be on top of everyone and marry me.

00:58:15.450 --> 00:58:19.430
And the water on top of her and on top of all of us.

00:58:19.630 --> 00:58:23.320
We'll swim like butterflies.

00:58:25.410 --> 00:58:29.670
- Castro's room, apartment 610. - Thank you.

00:58:36.840 --> 00:58:39.670
- Yes, yes, just a moment. - From the fashion house.

00:58:39.670 --> 00:58:44.300
And well, tell her that at 8:00 we have a press conference.

00:58:44.300 --> 00:58:47.180
- At 9:00 the recording. - At 10:00 the radio report.

00:58:47.180 --> 00:58:49.210
- And never rest. - Never!

00:58:49.210 --> 00:58:52.290
The Escalera has many little steps and there is no time to waste.

00:58:52.290 --> 00:58:54.290
Get used to living like a star.

00:58:54.290 --> 00:58:59.670
A large apartment of a large hotel, large houses, large meetings, large projects and a great rhythm.

00:59:00.220 --> 00:59:02.980
Publicity is the antecedent of success.

00:59:28.720 --> 00:59:29.920
This is called triumphing.

00:59:30.160 --> 00:59:33.080
Look, Susana, my true triumph will be to bring my parents...

00:59:33.240 --> 00:59:35.480
...and introduce them to your boyfriend, right?

00:59:35.680 --> 00:59:37.080
I don't have a boyfriend yet.

00:59:37.290 --> 00:59:40.760
Of course, now that I triumph, I'll have to keep my promise.

00:59:41.260 --> 00:59:44.800
- Mario or Gerardo? - Gerardo.

00:59:45.560 --> 00:59:51.700
- Go ahead. - The country is too small for us.

00:59:52.050 --> 00:59:55.150
In a moment, two German journalists will make a graphic note...

00:59:55.350 --> 00:59:57.400
...and announce our marriage.

00:59:58.130 --> 01:00:00.000
It will be the last and greatest...

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:03.880
- Is it so soon? - Don't think so.

01:00:03.900 --> 01:00:08.260
Well, then I'm going to get ready.

01:00:08.260 --> 01:00:10.610
- Excuse me. - You're dirty.

01:00:10.610 --> 01:00:27.510
Who's going to pay the bills at the hotel?

01:00:27.510 --> 01:00:30.000
I already told you.

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:31.820
The inheritance of Isabel de Castro.

01:00:31.820 --> 01:00:33.670
Isabel de Castro.

01:00:33.670 --> 01:00:36.190
Miss Isabel de Castro?

01:00:36.190 --> 01:00:38.020
Just a second, please.

01:00:38.020 --> 01:00:41.960
Hello?

01:00:41.960 --> 01:00:45.990
Yes? The gentlemen?

01:00:45.990 --> 01:00:48.200
- Get in. - Who is it?

01:00:48.200 --> 01:00:50.230
- The journalist. - Ah. The journalist.

01:00:50.230 --> 01:00:57.090
- Am I looking good? - Very good.

01:00:57.090 --> 01:00:58.200
Thank you.

01:01:02.910 --> 01:01:05.210
- Good evening. - Good evening. - Come in, come in. - Thank you.

01:01:05.210 --> 01:01:07.810
- Miss Isabel de Castro. - That's her.

01:01:07.810 --> 01:01:15.410
- What? The photographer... - No, no, no, no, no. No advertising.

01:01:15.410 --> 01:01:20.120
First we have to confirm the truth that Miss is Miss.

01:01:20.120 --> 01:01:23.010
- And what does Miss intend to be? - A florist.

01:01:23.010 --> 01:01:26.440
I'd say more like a bouquet of roses.

01:01:26.440 --> 01:01:29.920
But she is she.

01:01:31.080 --> 01:01:35.020
Yes, sir. It's her: Isabel de Castro, the winner of the contest.

01:01:35.120 --> 01:01:37.120
- It's not a contest. - What do you mean?

01:01:37.220 --> 01:01:38.630
It's a legacy.

01:01:38.740 --> 01:01:41.380
But you're not the European journalists.

01:01:41.480 --> 01:01:44.680
We're European, but not journalists.

01:01:44.780 --> 01:01:47.950
Allow me.

01:01:48.050 --> 01:01:50.430
González and González.

01:01:50.530 --> 01:01:54.960
From the law school: González, González and González.

01:01:55.060 --> 01:02:00.000
The other González stayed in Spain, serving the personal interests

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:04.000
- Isabel de Castro. - I don't want to know.

01:02:04.080 --> 01:02:06.240
Yes, you don't even know.

01:02:06.320 --> 01:02:08.130
It's a surprise we had prepared for you.

01:02:08.190 --> 01:02:11.050
The doctors were ahead of us, but we were waiting for the right moment.

01:02:11.130 --> 01:02:16.210
And this is the right moment to explain that we've been looking for you for a year.

01:02:16.290 --> 01:02:20.490
You're the benefactor of the fortune of Mr. Carmelo de Fuensalida.

01:02:20.570 --> 01:02:21.610
May he rest in peace.

01:02:21.690 --> 01:02:25.610
The great publicity of recent times gave us the clue we were looking for.

01:02:25.690 --> 01:02:28.660
- Are you sure it's for me? - We have all the documentation here.

01:02:28.740 --> 01:02:30.000
Open the folder.

01:02:30.060 --> 01:02:34.940
20 million pesetas, for Ms. Isabel de Castro.

01:02:34.940 --> 01:02:36.940
- That's a mistake. - No, no, no, it's 20 million.

01:02:36.940 --> 01:02:38.940
- Wait, wait. - Maybe it's more.

01:02:38.940 --> 01:02:44.940
- What do you know? It's 20 million. - 20 million, with 38 cents...

01:02:44.940 --> 01:02:46.890
...for Ms. Isabel de Castro.

01:02:46.890 --> 01:02:50.890
But, sir, listen, I'm not Isabel de Castro.

01:02:50.890 --> 01:02:53.160
- What did you say? - It's a joke.

01:02:53.160 --> 01:02:58.790
- How nice. - It's not a joke. I'm not.

01:02:58.790 --> 01:03:00.000
- But... - And who are you?

01:03:00.670 --> 01:03:04.010
When I arrived in Buenos Aires, the first thing I did was to change my name.

01:03:04.340 --> 01:03:06.340
It was funny and everyone made fun of him.

01:03:06.810 --> 01:03:10.660
Since I was born in Nochebuena, my parents thought of calling me "Natividad Oveja".

01:03:11.040 --> 01:03:14.510
- So you are... - Natividad Oveja!

01:03:14.510 --> 01:03:16.890
But then, Isabel de Castro!

01:03:16.890 --> 01:03:19.060
It was pretty and I put it on, like someone who trains a dress.

01:03:19.060 --> 01:03:21.000
- With that, no one was hurt! - Us!

01:03:21.000 --> 01:03:22.980
All our hope was called Isabel de Castro.

01:03:22.980 --> 01:03:26.250
And now, now, now we touch the bottom!

01:03:26.250 --> 01:03:28.130
A bottom full of algae and mollusks.

01:03:28.130 --> 01:03:29.670
I said that the inheritance...

01:03:30.060 --> 01:03:31.990
It was not a solution.

01:03:31.990 --> 01:03:33.600
Now I understand.

01:03:33.600 --> 01:03:35.960
So, I was nothing more than that, a solution.

01:03:35.960 --> 01:03:37.360
No, I'm going to explain.

01:03:37.360 --> 01:03:38.530
Don't explain anything to me.

01:03:38.530 --> 01:03:39.890
If I don't understand,

01:03:39.890 --> 01:03:42.660
all these favors were nothing more than an advance payment.

01:03:42.660 --> 01:03:45.000
Your love declarations, your haste to get married.

01:03:45.000 --> 01:03:45.920
Well, don't put it that way.

01:03:45.920 --> 01:03:47.900
We're all suffering from the blow.

01:03:47.900 --> 01:03:51.010
With the difference that it hurts you a fortune that's gone.

01:03:51.010 --> 01:03:53.290
And to me, an illusion that breaks.

01:03:53.290 --> 01:03:54.730
- Isabel! - Listen to me.

01:03:54.730 --> 01:03:55.910
I've heard it all.

01:03:55.910 --> 01:03:58.050
- Go away, go away! - But listen to me, listen to me.

01:03:58.050 --> 01:03:59.150
Go away.

01:03:59.150 --> 01:04:00.000
You didn't hear it.

01:04:01.340 --> 01:04:02.840
In what way did he escape?

01:04:04.830 --> 01:04:08.090
You know, Mr. Ernst, it's like asking a question.

01:04:08.340 --> 01:04:10.740
- What language does he speak? - He says he's here to make a note.

01:04:10.940 --> 01:04:12.740
As if it weren't the note of death.

01:04:13.540 --> 01:04:17.480
- Auf Wiedersehen. - Forget it.

01:04:17.930 --> 01:04:19.280
But, tell me...

01:04:20.260 --> 01:04:22.590
We've done a good job!

01:04:27.990 --> 01:04:29.860
Come on.

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:32.880
After all this mistake, I'll take you to fame.

01:04:33.440 --> 01:04:34.440
No.

01:04:34.750 --> 01:04:37.580
It's all been a bunch of false illusions.

01:04:37.700 --> 01:04:38.700
Your triumph didn't...

01:04:39.620 --> 01:04:40.620
It didn't exist.

01:04:40.940 --> 01:04:43.620
It was born from a lie, from a horrible lie.

01:04:43.780 --> 01:04:45.540
I don't want to see it ever again.

01:04:45.800 --> 01:04:47.150
Never again!

01:04:52.030 --> 01:05:00.000
- Extraordinary. - Watch Isabel's albums.

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:03.000
We're going to sell all of them. We're already floating!

01:05:03.000 --> 01:05:03.860
Then it's true.

01:05:03.860 --> 01:05:05.860
It means that in any case, Isabel de Castro

01:05:05.860 --> 01:05:08.900
is coming to be our salvation, eh?

01:05:30.410 --> 01:05:31.410
Let's see what's going on here.

01:05:31.490 --> 01:05:32.490
Excuse me.

01:05:33.220 --> 01:05:34.220
I want to know where Isabel is.

01:05:34.300 --> 01:05:35.800
- I'll go first. - And I'll stay here!

01:05:35.880 --> 01:05:38.800
And know that the one who's here is more than the one who's not!

01:05:38.880 --> 01:05:40.300
It's useless for you to look for her!

01:05:40.380 --> 01:05:42.800
Isabel has left, and you two are shameless!

01:05:42.880 --> 01:05:44.380
We don't know, but where is she?

01:05:44.480 --> 01:05:46.670
She left a few lines saying goodbye.

01:05:46.750 --> 01:05:48.150
- It can't be! - It is!

01:05:48.270 --> 01:05:51.320
And those who blame me, I want them, sir!

01:05:51.420 --> 01:05:53.560
- Dad! - Let's go.

01:06:10.170 --> 01:06:18.980
♪ The divine land bathes us ♪

01:06:18.980 --> 01:06:21.930
♪ With love ♪

01:06:21.930 --> 01:06:23.880
♪ The beauty of your sublimity ♪

01:06:23.880 --> 01:06:28.420
♪ From the sun to the sun ♪

01:06:30.640 --> 01:06:32.240
It was an incredible success.

01:06:32.440 --> 01:06:35.440
In no time, we've broken all known records.

01:06:35.640 --> 01:06:39.640
We've transformed a little hole-shaped boat into a luxurious ship.

01:06:39.840 --> 01:06:42.040
For me, it could have sunk.

01:06:42.240 --> 01:06:45.850
For what it's of use to us now, if at least we knew where it is.

01:06:46.050 --> 01:06:49.130
To tell you about your success. To make us forgive you.

01:06:49.620 --> 01:06:51.620
- May I? - Did you find it? Where is it?

01:06:51.820 --> 01:06:53.820
You don't deserve it, but anyway...

01:06:54.020 --> 01:06:55.940
- Let me go! - Let me go!

01:06:56.140 --> 01:06:58.450
Let me go!

01:07:02.620 --> 01:07:03.620
Come on!

01:07:57.680 --> 01:07:59.730
What's going on, Raffaella? What's taking you so long?

01:08:00.960 --> 01:08:03.370
so that they can be cured in thought.

01:08:03.540 --> 01:08:05.540
It's not thought, Mrs. Maria.

01:08:05.770 --> 01:08:07.550
Those are things of the heart.

01:08:07.880 --> 01:08:08.740
It will pass.

01:08:08.930 --> 01:08:11.210
It's time to get excited and to get excited again.

01:08:11.410 --> 01:08:13.050
And to think that tomorrow is your birthday

01:08:13.250 --> 01:08:15.020
and the whole town will come to greet you.

01:08:15.830 --> 01:08:16.880
Call her.

01:08:17.080 --> 01:08:18.340
Let's see if we cheer her up.

01:08:18.560 --> 01:08:19.830
- What's up? - Hello.

01:08:20.560 --> 01:08:23.360
Natividad, daughter, come, come.

01:08:30.410 --> 01:08:32.880
- What are you talking about? - Listen, Melati.

01:08:33.350 --> 01:08:36.500
I haven't heard you sing since I gave you the first lessons.

01:08:37.010 --> 01:08:40.950
- Father, I... - Sing, dear, sing.

01:08:42.550 --> 01:08:45.160
Forgive me, Father, I'm very sad.

01:08:45.730 --> 01:08:48.690
Don't you know that songs, like tears,

01:08:48.990 --> 01:08:52.720
- are used to vent your sorrows? - Of course, sing.

01:09:19.130 --> 01:09:22.150
wrapped in bitterness.

01:09:30.000 --> 01:09:55.670
the bitterness of love

01:10:58.760 --> 01:10:59.670
...to the world...

01:11:00.000 --> 01:11:02.000
You want to welcome us after all this?

01:11:02.000 --> 01:11:04.000
And now you think about that question?

01:11:04.000 --> 01:11:06.000
Oh, don't get carried away, don't get carried away. I serve as an ambassador.

01:11:06.000 --> 01:11:08.000
That in my country has another name.

01:11:08.000 --> 01:11:10.000
You are an angel.

01:11:10.000 --> 01:11:11.680
William! Let's see if we hurry.

01:11:11.680 --> 01:11:13.680
We will arrive this year.

01:11:13.680 --> 01:11:15.680
She's right, I don't know, buddy.

01:11:15.680 --> 01:11:17.680
But for the sake of the truth, we are there.

01:11:17.680 --> 01:11:19.680
I swear to you.

01:11:19.680 --> 01:11:21.680
Even if the horse dies.

01:11:21.680 --> 01:11:23.680
Arre! Arre, Molillo!

01:11:23.680 --> 01:11:26.210
Arre! Arre! Arre!

01:13:01.760 --> 01:13:21.230
- Why did they come? - Don't you suspect them?

01:13:21.230 --> 01:13:23.230
We finally found them.

01:13:23.230 --> 01:13:25.230
There are so many things we haven't been able to tell them.

01:13:25.230 --> 01:13:28.190
That's why we came. To apologize to them.

01:13:28.190 --> 01:13:30.000
To ask for their forgiveness.

01:13:32.200 --> 01:13:34.230
- What? - They always speak in plural.

01:13:35.850 --> 01:13:36.850
You're right.

01:13:36.880 --> 01:13:37.520
Why?

01:13:37.640 --> 01:13:39.880
If he's come with me, it's because I couldn't get him off me.

01:13:40.000 --> 01:13:40.760
It's not true.

01:13:42.000 --> 01:13:44.910
I've come because I love her, Isabel.

01:13:45.030 --> 01:13:45.720
Yes.

01:13:45.930 --> 01:13:46.740
No!

01:13:47.540 --> 01:13:49.900
The one who knows about these things, the one who loves her, is me.

01:13:50.020 --> 01:13:53.720
Please, Isabel, marry me.

01:14:07.740 --> 01:14:12.450
- Why didn't you tell me? - I had nothing to offer her.

01:14:35.530 --> 01:14:39.150
- You don't sing? - Me? No, sir.

01:14:39.350 --> 01:14:42.320
Good luck. It will prevent me from offering you a recording.

01:14:42.810 --> 01:14:47.170
I adore beautiful women who also don't sing.

01:14:47.370 --> 01:14:48.710
May I?

01:14:48.850 --> 01:14:53.720
I need to talk to you in a serene place, in a quiet place.

01:15:06.940 --> 01:15:07.940
for you, Nati.

01:15:16.990 --> 01:15:17.990
Yes!

01:15:31.400 --> 01:15:35.920
The earth is full of rye and the sky is blue.

01:16:00.640 --> 01:16:08.950
- Come on, come on, come on! - My daughter is going to sing!

01:16:08.950 --> 01:16:13.950
- I didn't tell you! - You were right, father! You were right!

01:16:13.950 --> 01:16:17.670
Little brunette, little brunette!

01:16:17.670 --> 01:16:28.470
You sad ones tell me that your Armita is having dinner.

01:16:28.470 --> 01:16:29.650
I don't know if...

01:16:40.010 --> 01:16:48.810
♪ Your eyes of light that you have cried ♪

01:16:48.810 --> 01:16:54.610
♪ That infinite gaze ♪

01:16:54.610 --> 01:16:57.550
♪ It loses you in the space ♪

01:16:57.550 --> 01:17:00.000
♪ You are saying: "Chiquita, what are you doing?" ♪

01:17:00.030 --> 01:17:02.030
What's going on with you?

01:17:02.030 --> 01:17:09.050
I'm telling you, little girl, what's going on with you?

01:17:09.050 --> 01:17:20.210
At the river bank, they raise the whistle

01:17:20.210 --> 01:17:25.710
Ay, ay, and they raise the whistle

01:17:35.240 --> 01:17:39.240
"Long live the state of the state, long live the state and its contours, contours full of life."

01:17:39.240 --> 01:17:45.240
"Morinitas, morinitas, ay, how will the peasant go?"

01:17:45.240 --> 01:17:48.790
"Are you suffering from love?"

01:18:04.320 --> 01:18:07.120
in papers that said

01:18:07.120 --> 01:18:10.290
a Tano

01:18:10.290 --> 01:18:17.230
that your ears

01:18:17.230 --> 01:18:21.860
broke in your fresh lips

01:18:21.860 --> 01:18:23.860
but your sorrow is my sorrow

01:18:23.860 --> 01:18:25.760
that for you I am

01:18:25.760 --> 01:18:27.720
weaning

01:18:27.720 --> 01:18:30.000
but your sorrow is my sorrow that

01:18:30.540 --> 01:18:33.110
I'm combing my hair

01:18:33.110 --> 01:18:44.010
I'm combing my hair

01:18:44.010 --> 01:18:54.090
I'm combing my hair

01:19:00.640 --> 01:19:01.540
Oh!
